msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:145
msgid "Root plugins and triggered plugins"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:147
msgid ""
"Some plugins should always be explicitly enabled on subprojects. We call "
"these root plugins, i.e. plugins that are _root_ nodes in the plugin "
"dependency graph."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:151
msgid ""
"Auto plugins also provide a way for plugins to automatically attach "
"themselves to projects if their dependencies are met. We call these "
"triggered plugins, and they are created by overriding the `trigger` method."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:155
msgid ""
"For example, we might want to create a triggered plugin that can append "
"commands automatically to the build. To do this, set the `requires` method "
"to return `empty`, and override the `trigger` method with `allRequirements`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:170
msgid ""
"The build user still needs to include this plugin in `project/plugins.sbt`, "
"but it is no longer needed to be included in `build.sbt`. This becomes more "
"interesting when you do specify a plugin with requirements. Let's modify the "
"`SbtLessPlugin` so that it depends on another plugin:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:185
msgid ""
"As it turns out, `PlayScala` plugin (in case you didn't know, the Play "
"framework is an sbt plugin) lists `SbtJsTaskPlugin` as one of its required "
"plugins. So, if we define a `build.sbt` with:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:192
msgid ""
"then the setting sequence from `SbtLessPlugin` will be automatically "
"appended somewhere after the settings from `PlayScala`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:194
msgid ""
"This allows plugins to silently, and correctly, extend existing plugins with "
"more features.  It also can help remove the burden of ordering from the "
"user, allowing the plugin authors greater freedom and power when providing "
"feature for their users."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:196
msgid "Controlling the import with autoImport"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:198
msgid ""
"When an auto plugin provides a `val`, `lazy val`, or `object` named "
"`autoImport`, the contents of the field are wildcard imported in `set`, "
"`eval`, and `*.sbt` files."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:210
msgid "\"greeting\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:211
msgid "\"say hello\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:220
msgid ""
"Typically, `autoImport` is used to provide new keys - `SettingKey`s, "
"`TaskKey`s, or `InputKey`s - or core methods without requiring an import or "
"qualification."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:223
msgid "Example Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:225
msgid "An example of a typical plugin:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:227
msgid ""
"````admonish example title=\"Plugin build.sbt\"\n"
"```scala\n"
"version := \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n"
"organization := \"com.example\"\n"
"homepage := Some(url(\"https://github.com/sbt/sbt-obfuscate\"))\n"
"\n"
"lazy val root = rootProject\n"
"  .enablePlugins(SbtPlugin)\n"
"  .settings(\n"
"    name := \"sbt-obfuscate\",\n"
"    pluginCrossBuild / sbtVersion := {\n"
"      scalaBinaryVersion.value match\n"
"        case \"3\" => \"2.0.0-RC10\" // set minimum sbt version\n"
"    }\n"
"  )\n"
"```\n"
"````"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:245
msgid ""
"````admonish example title=\"src/main/scala/sbtobfuscate/"
"ObfuscatePlugin.scala\"\n"
"```scala\n"
"package sbtobfuscate\n"
"\n"
"import sbt.*\n"
"import sbt.Keys.*\n"
"import sbt.CacheImplicits.given\n"
"import xsbti.HashedVirtualFileRef\n"
"\n"
"object ObfuscatePlugin extends AutoPlugin:\n"
"  // by defining autoImport, the settings are automatically\n"
"  // imported into user's `*.sbt`\n"
"  object autoImport:\n"
"    val obfuscate = taskKey[Seq[HashedVirtualFileRef]](\"Obfuscates files."
"\")\n"
"\n"
"    // configuration points, like built-in `version` and "
"`libraryDependencies`\n"
"    val obfuscateLiterals = settingKey[Boolean](\"Obfuscate literals.\")\n"
"  end autoImport\n"
"\n"
"  import autoImport.*\n"
"\n"
"  // This plugin is automatically enabled for projects which are JvmPlugin.\n"
"  override def trigger = allRequirements\n"
"\n"
"  // default values for the settings\n"
"  override lazy val globalSettings: Seq[Def.Setting[?]] = Seq(\n"
"    obfuscateLiterals := false,\n"
"  )\n"
"\n"
"  // default implementations for the tasks\n"
"  val baseObfuscateSettings: Seq[Def.Setting[?]] = Seq(\n"
"    obfuscate := {\n"
"      Obfuscate(sourcesVF.value, (obfuscate / obfuscateLiterals).value)\n"
"    },\n"
"  )\n"
"\n"
"  // a group of settings that are automatically added to projects.\n"
"  override lazy val projectSettings: Seq[Def.Setting[?]] =\n"
"    inConfig(Compile)(baseObfuscateSettings) ++\n"
"    inConfig(Test)(baseObfuscateSettings)\n"
"end ObfuscatePlugin\n"
"\n"
"object Obfuscate:\n"
"  def apply(\n"
"    sources: Seq[HashedVirtualFileRef],\n"
"    obfuscateLiterals: Boolean\n"
"  ): Seq[HashedVirtualFileRef] =\n"
"    // TODO obfuscate stuff!\n"
"    sources\n"
"end Obfuscate\n"
"```\n"
"````"
msgstr ""

