#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:333
msgid "Metabuild"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:335
msgid ""
"A metabuild is a project under `project/` folder. This project's classpath "
"is the classpath used for build definitions in `project/` and any `.sbt` "
"files in the project's base directory. It is also used for the `eval` and "
"`set` commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:340
msgid "Specifically,"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:342
msgid ""
"Managed dependencies declared by the metabuild are retrieved and are "
"available on the build definition classpath, just like for a normal project."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:345
msgid ""
"Unmanaged dependencies in `project/lib/` are available to the build "
"definition, just like for a normal project."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:347
msgid ""
"Sources in the `project/` project are the build definition files and are "
"compiled using the classpath built from the managed and unmanaged "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:350
msgid ""
"Project dependencies can be declared in `project/plugins.sbt` (similarly to "
"`build.sbt` file in a normal project) and will be available to the build "
"definitions."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:354
msgid ""
"The build definition classpath is searched for `sbt/sbt.autoplugins` "
"descriptor files containing the names of `sbt.AutoPlugin` implementations."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:358
msgid ""
"The `reload plugins` command changes the current build to the (root) "
"project's metabuild definition. This allows manipulating the metabuild "
"project like a normal subproject. `reload return` changes back to the "
"original build. Any session settings for the metabuild project that have not "
"been saved are dropped."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:364
msgid ""
"An auto plugin is a module that defines settings to automatically inject "
"into subprojects. Additionally, an auto plugin provides the following "
"feature:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:367
msgid ""
"Automatically import selective names to `.sbt` files and the `eval` and "
"`set` commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:368
msgid "Specify plugin dependencies to other auto plugins."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:369
msgid "Automatically activate itself when all dependencies are present."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:370
msgid ""
"Specify `projectSettings`, `buildSettings`, and `globalSettings` as "
"appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:372
msgid "Plugin dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:374
msgid ""
"Prior to the introduction of the `AutoPlugin` system in sbt 0.13.5, if a "
"plugin depended on the settings and tasks from another plugin, the build "
"users had to include the plugins in the right order. This became complicated "
"and error-prone as the number of plugins increased within an application."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:376
msgid ""
"An auto plugin can depend on other auto plugins and ensure these dependency "
"settings are loaded first."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:378
msgid ""
"Suppose we have the `SbtLessPlugin` and the `SbtCoffeeScriptPlugin`, which "
"in turn depends on the `SbtJsTaskPlugin`, `SbtWebPlugin`, and `JvmPlugin`. "
"Instead of manually activating all of these plugins, a project can just "
"activate the `SbtLessPlugin` and `SbtCoffeeScriptPlugin` like this:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:381
msgid "\".\""
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:385
msgid ""
"This will pull in the right setting sequence from the plugins in the right "
"order."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:387
msgid "Maven publishing convention"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/plugin.md:389
msgid ""
"sbt 2.x plugins are published to Maven layout repositories with `_sbt2_3` "
"suffix in its artifact name. For example, sbt-ci-release 1.11.2 is published "
"to the Central Repo as <https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/com/github/sbt/sbt-ci-"
"release_sbt2_3/1.11.2/>. This suffix is appended automatically by sbt, so "
"the `name` should just be called `sbt-ci-release` etc in `build.sbt`."
msgstr ""
